--TEST--
A class with a parent class cannot write `implements Revocable`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Only the class at the top of a chain may write `implements Revocable`.
class Base {}

class Mid extends Base {}

class Post extends Mid implements Revocable {}

echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/revocable-objects
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1001]: `Post` cannot implement `Revocable`, because its parent class `Mid` does not.
  --> case.nvs:7:35
%A
  = help: Write `implements Revocable` on `Base`, the class with no parent. `Post` then gets it too.

